<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n75725" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀττεύομαι</span></b> , 
			Att.
		 for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀσσεύομαι</span> (which does
		not occur), <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>divine from an
				ominous voice</i> or <i>sound</i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄσσα</span>)<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">, ὀττευομένη δὲ
			κάθηται</span> she sits <i>looking for omens</i>, of a lover,
				<i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Lys.</u>
				597
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ταῖς τούτων κληδόσι</span> by
			the cries of children, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.356e
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρὸς [κόρακος] βοήν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ael.
					<u>NA</u>
					1.48
				</span></i>
			: generally, <i>have forebodings of</i> a thing, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ μέλλον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plb.
					27.16.5
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τι περὶ τῶν ὅλων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					1.11.15
				</span></i>
			: c. (acc. et) inf., <i>augur that</i> . . ,
				<i><span class="en">
				Porph.
				<u>Antr.</u>
				33
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Lex.</u>
				19
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>regard as ominous</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὴν τύχην, τὸ
				ἔργον</span>, <i><span class="en">
				D.H.
				9.23
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				55
			</span></i>: hence, <i>deprecate as ill-omened</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πάντα τῦφον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					2.19
				</span></i>
			.—The 
				Act.
			
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀττεύουσιν</span> prob. f.l. in
			<i><span class="en">
				Ael.
				<u>NA</u>
				3.9
			</span></i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀπυίουσιν</span> cj. Pierson <i><span class="en">
				<u>Moer.</u>
				p.279
			</span></i> P.): <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κλῃδονίζομαι</span> was the
			equiv. Hellenic form, acc. to <i><span class="en">
				Moer.
			</span></i> l. c.</div>
